==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|knotty}}, {{m|enm|knotti}}, equivalent to {{suf|en|knot|y|id2=adjectival}}. Compare {{cog|nl|knoestig|t=knotty}}, {{cog|de|knotig|t=knotty}}, {{cog|sv|knutig}}, {{m|sv|knotig|t=knotty}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈnɒti/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-knotty.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{homophones|en|naughty}} {{qualifier|in accents with the [[w:cot-caught merger|cot-caught merger]]}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɒti|s=2}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|er|more}}

# [[full|Full]] of [[knot#Noun|knots]].
#: {{ux|en|a '''knotty''' pine}}
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Tempest|act=I|scene=ii|page=|column=|passage=If thou murmur'st, I will rend an oak / And peg thee in his '''knotty''' entrails till / Thou hast howl'd away twelve winters.}}
# [[complicated#Adjective|Complicated]] or [[tricky]]; [[complex]], [[difficult]].
#: {{synonyms|en|intricate|thorny}}
#: {{ux|en|a '''knotty''' problem}}
#* {{RQ:Swift Tale of a Tub|section=IX|sectionname=A Digression Concerning the Original, the Use and Improvement of Madness in a Commonwealth|pages=169–170|pageref=170|passage=The preſent Argument is the moſt abſtracted that ever I engaged in, it ſtrains my Faculties to their higheſt Stretch; and I deſire the Reader to attend with utmoſt perpenſity; For, I now proceed to unravel this '''knotty''' Point.}}

